\section{In a style file}{
A setting is its name, an equals sign and a value; a list of values is separated by commas; a \code{#} starts a note. The general settings come first, then each table type's under its heading:
\preformatted{
based.on = apa
font     = Arial

[regression]
fit.rows = r2, n
}
A general setting may also be set in a table type's section, for that table type only.
}
